  "note": "Two-column body page (verso, folio 272); the left margin column prints only the footer furniture since no 9.x section heading falls here, so all ten content blocks sit in the right text column. body_text_size_px=20.5 from this page's body cap heights. Block n=3 is an in-flow grey #6d6e71 sub-heading (major_heading). The bbox of figure n=8 (the acetylation/bromination/hydrolysis sequence) deliberately extends down to y 0.7761 to take in its four compound-name labels ('Aniline', 'N-Phenylethanamide (Acetanilide)', '(Major)', '4-Bromoaniline'), which A2 did not block separately - without them the figure would be cut off above its own captions. Likewise figure n=6 includes 'Aniline' and '2,4,6-Tribromoaniline'. No coloured panels, boxes or header band on this page - bare paper apart from the magenta/green scheme inks."
